ng and visual style unless they conflict with the identity reference.\n\nCreate a premium 3:4 vertical fashion concept sheet featuring a clearly adult woman with long sleek dark hair posing beside a bright orange wall. Preserve the uploaded portrait's facial identity and keep her clearly adult. Use a half-body editorial hero view with a relaxed, confident posture and one hand in a trouser pocket; let the layout also show inset details of the complete outfit.\n\nShe has long, sleek dark hair and soft-glam makeup. Style her in a fitted dark-brown cropped bandeau top under an oversized pastel mint-green blazer with structured shoulders, matching high-waisted wide-leg trousers, and an elegant silver chain detail attached to the blazer. Add silver drop earrings and layered silver necklaces. Keep the outfit polished and fully secure, with no wardrobe malfunction. Use cinematic natural sunlight and refined reflections along the orange wall and mint fabric.\n\nSurround the hero portrait with an airy professional fashion-blueprint layout: neat callout lines, small accessory/jewelry breakdowns, fabric-texture swatches, tailoring notes, a simple pose-analysis sketch and a few close-up insets of the silver jewelry and blazer chain. Keep the information hierarchy restrained and luxurious, with enough negative space and no clutter. Use only these exact readable labels: “BLAZER”, “TROUSERS”, “JEWELRY”, and “FABRIC”; all other annotation marks are abstract and unreadable. Modern Korean street-fashion editorial photography, realistic skin and fabric texture, high-detail concept-sheet finish without a specific resolution claim. No brand logo, extra text, watermark, plastic skin, distorted anatomy, extra fingers or excessive infographic clutter."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Text (User Prompt)", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#593930", "siz